}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{32}\\cdot {r}_{12}=(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}})\\cdot (2\\sqrt{3})=\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442811 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442815 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442811 1062 #uuid "24c95cd3-c302-51a3-abac-08bfbbb757dc" 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442811 1063 #edb/ref 17592186395100 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442812 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442813 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442812 1062 #uuid "2813bf88-52e1-5e7e-aeff-5a25b21a24b4" 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442812 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134354 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442813 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442811 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442813 1062 #uuid "668df193-99f3-547e-8195-6dfa92ee8c3d" 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442813 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415506 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442814 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442812 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442814 1062 #uuid "73796bfe-825e-5f2c-aa11-3af559c65185" 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442814 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442810 13194139534889 17592186045417 true] [17592186442815 1062 #uuid "aaef